>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Intro`

``` hol4
clasetLib.Intro : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as an unsafe introduction rule for one tactic invocation.

`Intro th` is logically equivalent to `th`, but carries a marker recognized
in a classical tactic's theorem list. The theorem is added to that call's
temporary rule set as an unsafe introduction rule. Introduction rules match
their conclusion against a goal and turn their premises into subgoals.

An unmarked theorem in the theorem list has the same unsafe-introduction
classification. The safe classical tactics accept this classification but
do not apply unsafe rules. Use `SIntro th` when `SAFE_TAC`, `CLARIFY_TAC`, or a
safe step tactic should use the rule.

The corresponding persistent attribute is argument-free `[intro]`. Despite
its plain spelling it is unsafe; `[sintro]` denotes the safe classification.

### Failure

Constructing `Intro th` does not validate the rule. A tactic that consumes
the marker may fail if `th` cannot be converted to introduction-rule form.

### Example

The following two theorem lists classify `my_rule` identically:

``` hol4
classicalLib.SAFE_TAC [clasetLib.Intro my_rule]
classicalLib.SAFE_TAC [my_rule]
```

Neither call applies `my_rule`, because `SAFE_TAC` uses only safe rules.

